What are Router object and RouterMethods and how to implement them?
===============================================================
→A Router object is used to group related routes.
→ First, we create an instance of the router using the Express instance by calling the Router() method.
→This method returns a router object.Using this router object, we can define routes using methods like get(), post(), put(), and delete().
→ In these methods, the first parameter is the URL path and the second parameter is the route handler function.
→ By separating the routing logic this way, we can define routes in a separate file and then import the router into the main application instead of writing all routes using app.get() or app.post().
const express = require("express");
const router = express.Router();   → router object
Router methods : 
router.get(), post,put..
router.use() (for middleware)